GBR_COLS = ["GBR-ID", "Rule Statement", "Applies To", "Rationale", "Enforced By"]
GBR = [
["GBR-01","The interface is Vietnamese. Dates are dd/mm/yyyy, times are 24-hour HH:mm, and all times use the gym's time zone Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh (UTC+7). Enumerated values are stored in English and displayed in Vietnamese.","All screens","Staff and members are Vietnamese; one time zone avoids off-by-one-day errors in expiry and attendance.","The system automatically on every screen and stored time"],
["GBR-02","All amounts are whole Vietnamese dong. Catalogue prices already include VAT — exactly what the customer sees and pays. The VAT rate (P-10) is copied into each order, and the VAT amount is computed as price × VAT ÷ (100 + VAT), rounded to the dong. Screens show VAT as a breakdown, never as an extra charge.","All sales, payment and report screens","Customers pay exactly the listed price; VAT is shown for tax reporting without changing the price.","The system automatically on every price, order and report"],
["GBR-03","The end date of every package, freeze, voucher and report period is the last valid day. A one-month package starting 05/09 ends on 05/10 and can be used for the whole of 05/10; the next package starts 06/10. If the target day does not exist in the target month (start 30/01 or 31/01), the last day of that month is used.","All dated records","Customers get the full last day they paid for; all modules count dates the same way.","The system automatically when computing end dates"],
["GBR-04","Business limits are parameters P-01…P-23 stored in SystemConfigs. A change applies only to records created afterwards: each order keeps the VAT rate and payment deadline it was created with, and each subscription keeps the freeze allowance (P-01) and swap allowance (P-08) copied at sale. Values that are fixed in the system and not parameters: the 13:00 shift boundary (GBR-38), the 15-minute PT-sale hold (BR-93) and the 5-minute VNPay link validity (CBR-70).","All modules","The Manager can adjust business limits without a code change; existing orders stay as sold.","The system automatically, reading SystemConfigs when a record is created"],
["GBR-05","No business record is physically deleted; \"delete\" switches it to Inactive (or Retired / Withdrawn), so history stays intact. The only physical deletions are: a Pending leave request withdrawn by its owner (BR-83), a body measurement deleted by the customer (BR-89), time slots that were created only for an expired or released PT-sale hold (BR-93), and the Exercise cache refreshed from wger (BR-92).","All entities","History, revenue and tax records must stay complete and traceable; the exceptions hold no financial or audit value.","The system automatically on every delete action"],
["GBR-06","A record cannot be deactivated while another active record still refers to it. Exception: a catalogue package can be switched to \"Stop selling\" (Inactive) while customers still use it — running orders and subscriptions are unaffected (CBR-97).","All entities","Prevents orphan or broken references (e.g. a PT with future sessions) without blocking the catalogue.","The system automatically before every deactivation"],
["GBR-07","Every sensitive action — price or catalogue change, account action, contact or password change, deletion, approval or rejection, cancellation, session handling, shift action and every background-job state change — is written to the audit log in the same transaction as the change.","All modules","Lets the Admin trace who changed money, accounts and decisions.","The system automatically on every sensitive action"],
["GBR-08","Each audit line reads as a plain sentence: who – in which role – did what – to what – from which value to which value – when – why. Background-job lines have no account and no role. Passwords and verification codes are never written. Only the Admin can read the log.","Audit log","The Admin can read the log without technical knowledge.","The system automatically when writing the audit log"],
["GBR-09","Every negative or corrective staff action — rejecting a request, cancelling a session or order, deleting a profile, voiding, a cash variance, approving a leave request after it started (BR-86) — requires a written reason of 5–500 characters, stored with the record and in the audit log. Customers are never asked for a reason.","All approval and cancellation actions","Negative decisions must be explainable to customers and staff.","The system on submit (reason required, 5–500 characters)"],
["GBR-10","Each action can be performed only by the role the user is working in (Guest, Customer, PT, Receptionist, Manager, Admin) according to the permission matrix; users see and change only the data their role allows. A user who holds several roles chooses one after signing in (CBR-113).","All screens","Each role sees and does only what its job requires.","The system on every page and request (role filter per URL area)"],
["GBR-11","PT slots, single-session bookings and check-ins must fall within the opening hours of that day (P-19 or the date's exception). PT package sessions are generated on every chosen weekday of the term, including closed days, and must then be rescheduled by the PT (CBR-56).","Scheduling, booking, check-in","Nothing can be booked or used while the gym is closed.","The system automatically on every time-based action"],
["GBR-12","Everyone who uses a service — members, dependants and walk-ins — has exactly one active customer profile.","All customer-facing features","Avoids duplicate members and split purchase history.","The system on profile creation (phone/email duplicate check)"],
["GBR-13","Every rule checked on a screen is checked again on the server; the server never trusts values sent by the interface (identity, prices, ids). Competing actions on the same record are resolved by locks and conditional updates in one transaction — the later request is refused with a reload message.","All modules","Values sent from the browser can be altered.","The system on the server for every request"],
["GBR-14","Time-based rules run without user action. Daily at 00:05 (UTC+7), in order: JOB-01 freeze resume, JOB-02 package expiry, JOB-03 day-pass expiry, JOB-04 PT session auto-close, JOB-08 gym-access reminder. Every minute: JOB-05 overdue online orders, JOB-06 timed-out transactions, JOB-07 leave reminder. A daily job that fails on a database error is retried every 5 minutes. Expired PT-sale holds are released when the PT-sale screen is next used (BR-93).","All time-based states","Statuses stay correct even when nobody is at the counter.","Background job scheduler"],
["GBR-15","Verification codes, temporary passwords and security alerts are sent by email only; there is no SMS. In-app notifications (bell) reach only accounts that are Active; Dependent profiles have no account and are informed outside the system.","Notifications, sign-up, recovery, counter account","Email is free and reliable; SMS is out of scope.","The system when sending codes and notifications"],
["GBR-16","Refunds, invoices / e-invoices and cost of goods are handled outside the system; the system only records what is needed to trigger or reconcile them (the Manager confirms a refund in the system after paying it — BR-81).","Sales, payment, reports","Keeps the project scope; accounting is done in the gym's existing tools.","Business process (outside the system)"],
["GBR-17","Required fields are marked *. Validation runs when leaving a field and again on submit; each error appears in red under its field. An error returned by the server is shown when the page opens and disappears as soon as the user corrects the field.","All forms","Users fix errors before submitting, without losing input.","The system on blur, on submit and on page load"],
["GBR-18","Lists are paged after search and filters are applied, and changing a filter returns to page 1. The page size depends on the screen: management lists (leave requests, maintenance requests, deletion requests, shift history, system transactions) show 10 rows by default with a 10 / 20 / 50 selector — any other value falls back to 10; customer transaction history shows 20 per page; the Exercise Library 12 cards; package selection 8 cards; the public blog 6 posts; check-in and freeze customer search 10 rows; the Receptionist facility catalogue 30 groups. Suggestion boxes are capped (PT-sale customer search 8, counter-sale customer search 20, bell 10, dashboard 5). Calendar and summary screens are not paged (My Bookings, My PT Sessions, PT schedule, PT dashboard, facility master–detail, package catalogue). A page number outside the range is moved to the nearest valid page.","All lists","Each screen shows the amount of data its users actually scan; long lists stay fast.","The system on every list"],
["GBR-19","Keywords are trimmed, case-insensitive and diacritic-insensitive (\"nguyen\" matches \"Nguyễn\", \"do mai\" matches \"Đỗ Thị Mai\"); a phone number may be typed with spaces.","All search boxes","Vietnamese names are found whether typed with or without diacritics.","The system on every search box"],
["GBR-20","Filters combine with AND; \"Clear filters\" restores the defaults. An invalid filter value in the URL is ignored and the default is used — it never causes an error page.","All lists","Predictable, narrowing filters.","The system on every filtered list"],
["GBR-21","An empty list shows a short message: nothing yet, no result for the search, or no data in the chosen period. A loading error is shown as an error with a reload action, never as an empty list.","All lists and reports","The user knows the list is empty rather than broken.","The system on every list and report"],
["GBR-22","The submit button is disabled while a request is processed; success shows a toast; on error the form keeps the user's input.","All forms","Prevents double submission and lost input.","The system on every form"],
["GBR-23","Irreversible or destructive actions (delete, cancel, void, reject, deactivate, retire, publish, release a hold) ask for confirmation first; a rejection or cancellation confirmation also collects the reason.","All destructive actions","Prevents irreversible mistakes.","The system before every destructive action"],
["GBR-24","Leaving a form with unsaved changes asks the user to confirm (MSG28).","All forms marked as editable","Prevents losing typed data.","The system when leaving a form"],
["GBR-25","Fields the current user may not edit are shown read-only, with a hint saying who can change them.","All forms","The user knows why a field is locked and whom to ask.","The system on every form"],
["GBR-26","Dates, slots or options that break a rule are shown but disabled or marked, with a short reason (and the full reason on hover or tap).","All date, slot and option pickers","The user sees why an option is unavailable.","The system on every picker"],
["GBR-27","Time-limited states (online payment deadline, PT-sale hold, verification code, resend wait, temporary lock) show an mm:ss countdown; the page refreshes when it reaches zero.","Payment, PT sale, sign-in, verification","The user knows how long a hold or code is still valid.","The system on every time-limited state"],
["GBR-28","Green = active / successful, amber = pending / held / needs attention, red = rejected / cancelled / failed, grey = inactive / expired / past — the same on every screen. A status is never shown by colour alone: it always has a label (and on calendars a distinct shape).","All status badges","Statuses are recognised at a glance, also by colour-blind users.","The system on every status badge"],
["GBR-29","Amounts are right-aligned with a thousand separator and \"đ\"; totals show \"incl. VAT x%\".","All amounts","Amounts are easy to read and compare.","The system on every money field"],
["GBR-30","Password fields are masked with a show/hide (eye) toggle.","Sign-in, sign-up, recovery, account","Prevents shoulder surfing while allowing a check of what was typed.","The system on every password field"],
["GBR-31","When the sign-in session expires (2 hours of inactivity), the user signs in again and returns to the same screen.","All signed-in screens","Users do not lose their place after a time-out.","The system on every authenticated page"],
["GBR-32","If a record changed since it was opened, saving is refused and the user is asked to reload (MSG22).","All edit forms","Prevents one user silently overwriting another.","The system on save (row version or status check)"],
["GBR-33","Exports contain exactly the rows matching the current search and filters (system transactions → .xlsx; operational report → CSV of the displayed view).","Lists and reports with export","The export matches what the user sees.","The system on every export"],
["GBR-34","Success toasts disappear after a few seconds; error toasts stay until closed. Notifications in the bell keep a read / unread state (read time), can be marked read one by one or all at once.","All screens","Feedback is visible but not intrusive.","The system on every toast and notification"],
["GBR-35","Every main screen works at phone (390 px), tablet (768 / 1024 px) and desktop (1440 px) widths without horizontal page scrolling; calendars switch to a one-day or list view on small screens.","All screens","Customers and PTs use phones; staff use desktops and tablets.","The system (responsive layout)"],
["GBR-36","Explanations of a screen are shown in an (i) hint box next to the title or block, opened by click, tap or keyboard and closed with Escape or a click outside — not as permanent subtitles.","All main screens","Screens show data first; help stays one click away.","The system (shared hint box component)"],
["GBR-37","Texts shown to users never contain internal rule codes (CBR-, BR-, DBR-, GBR-); parameter codes P-xx may appear on Manager configuration screens. All messages come from the System Messages catalogue (section 6).","All screens","Users read plain Vietnamese; rule codes belong to the specification.","The system (message catalogue)"],
["GBR-38","Each day is split into two shifts at 13:00: the morning shift runs from the opening time of the day (default 05:30, P-19) to 13:00 and the afternoon shift from 13:00 to the closing time (default 22:00). A slot, session or leave belongs to a shift by its start time (before 13:00 = morning). The same boundary is used by leave requests, the CBR-83 check, PT slot locking during leave, PT-sale shift assignment, the PT schedule divider and Receptionist shifts.","Leave, PT schedule, PT sale, shifts","One boundary everywhere avoids a session counted in two shifts.","The system (one shared constant)"],
["GBR-39","The account badge on every screen shows the full name, initials avatar (or uploaded avatar) and a role code: KH-nnnn Hội viên, PT-nnnn Huấn luyện viên, LT-nnnn Lễ tân, QL-nnnn Quản lý, QT-nnnn Quản trị viên. Only the prefix changes for display; the stored codes stay KH-nnnn / NV-nnnn (DBR-09).","All signed-in screens","Users always see which role they are working in.","The system on every signed-in page"],
]
